# Build context for the api/worker image (see Dockerfile). Anything not needed to run
# `python -m server.server` / `python -m server.worker` / `alembic upgrade head` stays out.
#
# Secrets: `.env` in this repo is a symlink to `.env.local` (verified: `ls -la .env` shows
# `.env -> .env.local`). Docker's default .dockerignore matcher follows symlink *names*, not
# targets, so both the link and the real file must be listed explicitly or the target leaks
# under the link's name. Both patterns are below.

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.venv/
server/venv/
*.egg-info/

# Env / secrets — never bake these into an image
.env
.env.*
.env.local
!.env.example

# Frontend — this image is backend-only (api + worker); no web/ service is built from it
web/

# Local file-store data (pre-Postgres state, gitignored, and irrelevant to a stateless image)
server/data/
data/

# VCS / editor / CI
.git/
.github/
.gitignore
.claude/

# Caches
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/

# Docs, plan, notes — not needed at runtime
docs/
*.md

# Node
node_modules/
